{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker","name":"algebra-step-checker","description":"A math tutor that checks every line of your work, pinpoints the first wrong step, names the misconception and coaches with Socratic hints.","category":"Education","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T04:05:30Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:50:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/algebra-step-checker/","topics":["education","github-pages","javascript","math","mathjs"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/algebra-step-checker/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.399Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.399Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.399Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.399Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A math tutor that checks every line of your work, pinpoints the first wrong step, names the misconception and coaches with Socratic hints.","Most tutors only check the final answer. Step Check verifies your reasoning line by line. Each step is parsed with math.js and compared to the previous one numerically: expressions must agree at random sample points, and equations must be scalar multiples of each other or keep exactly the same solution set (found by sign-change scanning, bisection and ternary search for double roots). The first wrong step is classified locally (sign error? off by a constant? lost solutions?). The AI then names the specific misconception, gives three progressively stronger Socratic hints and finally the…"],"features":["Line-by-line verification of algebra: expressions, equations and 'x = 2 or x = 3' answer sets","Numerical equivalence engine: random-point testing, proportionality test, root finding with bisection + ternary search","Local error classification (sign flip, constant offset, scale factor, lost/extra solutions)","KaTeX-rendered steps with / status and evidence","AI misconception tagging against a fixed taxonomy (exponent over addition, partial division, sign moves …)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9606c61323786798afdcb1c6f437dd12ef1eb40fc4fe16cb64996ba0e4fbeb81","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.469Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.469Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A math tutor that checks every line of your work, pinpoints the first wrong step, names the misconception and coaches with Socratic hints.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"index.html is the public home page, login.html handles accounts and app.html is the app.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9606c61323786798afdcb1c6f437dd12ef1eb40fc4fe16cb64996ba0e4fbeb81","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.470Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T03:50:21Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/algebra-step-checker/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.470Z","hash":"9606c61323786798afdcb1c6f437dd12ef1eb40fc4fe16cb64996ba0e4fbeb81","originalBytes":5581,"storedBytes":5581,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["page","src","misconception","step","app","every","lib","tests","settings","solutions","browser","error","generated","must","only","practice","profile","runs","solver","accounts","bisection","check","core.js","each","equations","finding","functions","index.html","provider","root","roots","search","sign","socratic","styles","ternary","testing","unit","aimed","algebra-step-checker","answer","app.html","bash","box","build","calls","checks","classification","constant","correct","covered","dom"